{"parentUuid":"bb4e395c-5e09-45bd-87bc-cf23a762c6e3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Xv1anU6QKsQsxYb1KVujDL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20242,"cache_read_input_tokens":59913,"output_tokens":4873,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20242,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":4873,"cache_read_input_tokens":59913,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20242,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20242},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaUNQKxj5FMSk8BYwazcP","type":"assistant","uuid":"e038c1ad-fcb0-4eaa-836b-f7fdbbd712fa","timestamp":"2026-04-27T13:40:17.896Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"b8f6d643-d50f-43cc-b9e7-b5dfa6939c04","version":"2.1.119","gitBranch":"explain-external-summary-providers"}
{"parentUuid":"e038c1ad-fcb0-4eaa-836b-f7fdbbd712fa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Xv1anU6QKsQsxYb1KVujDL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# PR #1044 Review: Support external agents to generate summary in `entire explain`\n\n## Overview\n\nExtends the summary-generation pipeline so external `entire-agent-*` plugins that advertise `capabilities.text_generator` can serve as summary providers for both `entire explain --generate` and the post-commit auto-summarize hook. Also adds an opt-in `compact_transcript` fallback path that lets external agents reduce their own transcripts into a Claude-compatible JSONL format the summarizer understands, with a follow-up redaction pass before the bytes touch the LLM.\n\n+515 / -28 across 12 files. Branch is up to date with `main` (merged in `6ceefd734`).\n\n## What looks good\n\n- **Provider availability split is the right shape.** `isSummaryProviderAvailable` (`explain_summary_provider.go:307`) bypasses PATH checks for external agents — they were already proven runnable by discovery — while keeping the PATH check for built-ins. This matches how `external.IsExternal` is used elsewhere.\n- **Discovery is lazy and bounded.** `discoverSummaryProviderIfMissing` only triggers `external.DiscoverAndRegister` when the configured provider isn't already registered (`explain_summary_provider.go:280`), and the test at `explain_summary_provider_test.go:382` enforces this with `t.Fatal` if discovery is called for a registered provider. Good guardrail against accidentally turning every config read into a discovery scan.\n- **Redaction is enforced at the right boundary.** `maybeCompactExternalTranscriptForSummary` runs the external compactor's output through `redact.JSONLBytes` *before* passing it to the summarizer (`explain.go:200`). The follow-up comment at `explain.go:230` is now accurate (\"either read from checkpoint storage … or replaced by external compact output redacted before use\"). The dedicated test `TestMaybeCompactExternalTranscriptForSummary_RedactsExternalOutput` proves a 32-char secret never leaks.\n- **Lint cleanup is the better fix.** Replacing scattered `//nolint:ireturn` comments with a one-time `.golangci.yaml` allowlist (lines 9, 12, 17 of the diff) is the conventional approach in this repo and removes four lint suppressions.\n- **Interface-return reordering** in `buildSummaryGenerator` (`manual_commit_condensation.go:671`) — checking `AsTextGenerator` before the PATH check — is logically tighter and avoids the PATH probe for incapable agents.\n- **`IsExternal` now handles both wrapper types** (`capabilities.go:151`). Without this, an external agent with `protected_files` would have been incorrectly treated as built-in and rejected by the new availability path.\n\n## Issues & risks\n\n### 1. `setup.go` silently flips a global setting (medium)\n\n`updateSummaryGenerationSettings` now sets `s.ExternalAgents = true` whenever the chosen summary provider is external (`setup.go:179`). This is a reasonable convenience, but:\n\n- It changes a setting outside the user's explicit instruction (they asked for `--summarize-provider`, not `--external-agents`).\n- There's no message in the success output saying \"also enabled external_agents\".\n- If the user later runs `entire configure --summarize-provider <built-in>`, `external_agents` stays `true` — there's no symmetric \"disable when no longer needed\" branch. That's defensible (other features may depend on it), but worth a note in `--help` or the success message.\n\nSuggest at minimum printing a one-line notice when this happens.\n\n### 2. The `transcriptHasSummaryContent` double-check is a quiet failure mode\n\n`maybeCompactExternalTranscriptForSummary` calls `transcriptHasSummaryContent` twice (`explain.go:142, 209`). If the first check passes the original transcript through unchanged, fine. If the post-compact/post-redact check fails, the function silently returns the *original* transcript (`explain.go:210`) — meaning summary generation will then fail downstream with a less informative error. A `logging.Debug(... \"compact transcript still has no summary content\")` line at the rejection site would help debugging without changing behavior.\n\n### 3. `BuildCondensedTranscriptFromBytes` fallback semantics are subtle\n\nThe new fallback in `summarize.go:148-156` does:\n\n1. Try Claude parser; if it errors, try compact parser; if that fails, return the original Claude error.\n2. If Claude succeeds but returns 0 entries, *also* try compact and return its output unconditionally.\n\nStep 2 is the surprising one: we replace a successful-but-empty Claude parse with whatever the compact parser yields, even if compact returns a non-empty list of entries that happen to be wrong because the bytes really were Claude format. In practice this is unlikely to matter (genuine empty Claude transcripts are rare and a compact parser on Claude bytes will usually error), but a quick comment on intent would prevent future regressions.\n\n### 4. Tests can't run in parallel — silent global registry mutation\n\nSeveral new tests carry comments like *\"Cannot use t.Parallel() because external agent discovery mutates the package-level agent registry\"* (`explain_summary_provider_test.go:271`, `explain_test.go:455`, `manual_commit_condensation_test.go:755`). This is consistent with existing patterns but is technical debt: the agent registry is effectively a process-global singleton that any test calling `external.DiscoverAndRegister` will pollute. Not a blocker for this PR, but it's three more tests now stuck on the slow path. Worth a follow-up issue to make discovery accept an injectable registry.\n\n### 5. Temp file lifecycle in `maybeCompactExternalTranscriptForSummary`\n\nMinor: at `explain.go:160-188`, on the close-fail branch the deferred `os.Remove(tmpPath)` runs after `tmpFile.Close()` returns an error, which is fine on macOS/Linux. The double-close protection (`_ = tmpFile.Close()` after Write failure) is correct. Just confirm CI covers Windows if anything in the test matrix targets it (I don't believe it does for this project, so no action needed).\n\n### 6. Error message wording\n\nThe new error in `explain_summary_provider.go:272` is long (\"install claude, codex, gemini, cursor, or copilot, install an external entire-agent-* plugin that declares text_generator, or set summary_generation.provider in settings\"). Consider splitting the \"install one of …\" and \"or install an external plugin\" into two lines so terminals don't wrap awkwardly. Pure polish.\n\n## Test coverage\n\nStrong. The new tests cover:\n- External provider configured explicitly (`TestResolveCheckpointSummaryProvider_ConfiguredExternalProvider`)\n- External provider from auto-discovery + `--summarize-provider` setting (`TestConfigureCmd_SummarizeProvider_ExternalEnablesExternalAgents`)\n- Redaction of external compact output (`TestMaybeCompactExternalTranscriptForSummary_RedactsExternalOutput`) — using a real 32-char secret token, which is the right bar\n- Built-in providers don't trigger discovery (`TestBuildSummaryGenerator_BuiltInProviderSkipsExternalDiscovery`)\n- Compact transcript fallback parsing (`TestBuildCondensedTranscriptFromBytes_CompactTranscriptFallback`)\n- `IsExternal` covers the protected-files wrapper (`TestIsExternal_WithProtectedFilesWrapper`)\n\nGaps I'd consider adding:\n- The \"compact succeeds but yields no summary content\" branch (the silent fallback at `explain.go:210`) is currently uncovered.\n- No test for the `agent.AsTranscriptCompactor(ag) → false` early-out path (`explain.go:155`).\n\n## Security\n\n- Redaction is preserved on every path that feeds bytes to the LLM. Verified by the new test.\n- External binaries are still invoked via the existing `entire-agent-<name>` discovery mechanism, no new exec surface.\n- Temp file uses `os.CreateTemp` (mode 0600) — fine for the JSONL transcript that is already redacted.\n\n## Performance\n\n- Auto-summarize path adds an extra `agent.Get` + possibly a `DiscoverAndRegister` call when the configured provider isn't registered. Discovery is bounded to `entire-agent-*` PATH entries and only triggered on cache miss. Acceptable.\n- For external compact: extra disk write of the redacted transcript + an external process invocation, but only when the original transcript can't be parsed by the built-in summarize logic (`transcriptHasSummaryContent` short-circuits the common case). Reasonable cost for the fallback.\n\n## Recommendation\n\n**Approve with minor follow-ups.** The architecture is clean, redaction is in the right place, and tests cover the riskiest paths. I'd ask for:\n\n1. Add a `logging.Debug` at `explain.go:210` for the silent-fallback-after-redact case.\n2. A one-line user-visible notice when `--summarize-provider <external>` flips `external_agents` to `true` (`setup.go:179`).\n3. A short comment on the \"Claude succeeds but 0 entries → try compact\" branch in `summarize.go:151` explaining intent.\n\nNothing blocking."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20242,"cache_read_input_tokens":59913,"output_tokens":4873,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20242,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":4873,"cache_read_input_tokens":59913,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20242,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20242},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaUNQKxj5FMSk8BYwazcP","type":"assistant","uuid":"af0afed7-5232-4566-abe1-436168cf7ce6","timestamp":"2026-04-27T13:41:07.485Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"b8f6d643-d50f-43cc-b9e7-b5dfa6939