{"parentUuid":"3063133a-a31a-407a-960c-1146d0e50c41","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_014XgifQ3JCSNJuYH86igpUc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sounds right overall. A few shaping calls worth deciding before code:\n\n- **`revoke` over `delete`.** The OpenAPI uses \"revoke\" and that's the correct verb here — it kills the token server-side, not just locally. `delete` would imply local-only.\n- **Flat under `auth`, not nested under `auth tokens`.** `entire auth list` / `auth revoke <id>` / `auth revoke --current` reads better than `auth tokens list` unless you anticipate other auth resources (sessions, devices) eventually.\n- **Aliases via cobra `Aliases` field.** Keep top-level `entire login` / `entire logout` working forever — `gh`, `docker`, `glab` all do this, and breaking muscle memory for a reorg is rude. The way to do this in cobra is to register both the namespaced command and a top-level alias that delegates to the same `RunE`, not via the `Aliases` array (which only handles same-level renames).\n- **Consider `auth status` too.** Shows current base URL + whether a token is present (without printing it) + maybe `GET /api/v1/auth/me`. Fills the \"am I logged in and as whom\" gap that's currently invisible.\n\nMain tradeoff: doing the full reshuffle now is a bigger surface change than just adding `auth list` / `auth revoke` next to the existing `login` / `logout`. If you're not sure the namespace will earn its keep, you could ship the two new commands flat (`entire list-tokens`, `entire revoke-token`) and only group later — but I'd just do the `auth` group now since you clearly know where this is heading.\n\nWant me to plan the command surface concretely (flag names, output format for `list`, `--current` vs positional id for `revoke`) before I start writing?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":136,"cache