o <baseURL> as @<github_login>. Token stored in OS keychain.\"\n- Logged in, 401 → \"Token in keychain for <baseURL> is no longer valid. Run `entire login` to re-authenticate.\"\n\n**Implementation plan**\n1. Add the three `api.Client` methods + tests.\n2. Extract `runLogin` / `runLogout` so they can be registered under both `auth.X` and top-level — minimal refactor, just construct two `cobra.Command`s pointing at the same handler.\n3. Add `auth.go` with the group + new subcommands.\n4. Register everything on root.\n\nTwo things I want to confirm before I start:\n\n1. **Is `GET /api/v1/auth/me` reachable with bearer auth?** It's used by the frontend with session cookies; if it's session-only on the backend, `auth status` won't be able to verify identity over a CLI bearer token and we'd need a different endpoint (or a tiny backend change). Want me to check the entire.io backend handler, or assume bearer works and let CI/QA catch it?\n\n2. **`auth revoke` with no args** — error, or default to `--current`? I lean error (explicit > implicit, especially for destructive ops); `entire logout` is the easy path for \"revoke mine.\""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":771,"cache_read_input_tokens":146521,"output_tokens":3111,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":771,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":3111,"cache_read_input_tokens":146521,"cache_creation_input_tokens":771,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":771},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaUhwbpJ14SowKQaBoeJt","type":"assistant","uuid":"a6980242-6053-4f69-b64c-d88ae7678baa","timestamp":"2026-04-27T17:56:50.679Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/deve