ing the caller's request.` is fine (explains why), but `auth.go:259` `// Header row.` and `auth.go:268` `// Body rows.` just restate the obvious WHAT. Drop them.\n\n**6. Stringly-typed magic values** — `auth.go:209-210` (`\"-\"`), `auth.go:291` (`\"-\"`), `auth.go:304` (`\"never\"`), `auth.go:315` (`\"just now\"`). These appear in tests (`auth_test.go:167,226`). Promote to package-level consts (`placeholderDash`, `lastUsedNever`, `lastUsedJustNow`) so test assertions and production share a source of truth.\n\n**7. `defaultListTokens` / `defaultRevokeTokenByID` / `defaultRevokeCurrentToken` shape** — `auth.go:62-68, 395-400`, `logout.go:36-41`. All three are 3-line `api.NewClient(token).X()` thunks wrapping with `fmt.Errorf`. The wrapping is redundant: `ListTokens`, `RevokeToken`, `RevokeCurrentToken` already prefix errors with `\"list tokens:\"`, `\"revoke token X:\"`, `\"revoke current token:\"` (auth_tokens.go:31,51,66). The thunks just double-wrap. Either delete the wrappers and pass method values directly via small adapter (e.g. `func(ctx, t) ([]Token, error) { return api.NewClient(t).ListTokens(ctx) }`), or remove the redundant wrapping in api/auth_tokens.go.\n\n**8. `runAuthRevoke` parameter sprawl** — `auth.go:402-410`. 8 params is a smell, but the real issue is they're three concerns: I/O (`outW, errW`), dependencies (`store, revokeByID, revokeCurrent, baseURL`), inputs (`id, current`). Group deps into a struct (`authRevokeDeps`) like other commands in this codebase often do. Bonus: `runAuthRevoke` calls `runLogout` and so depends on a `logoutRevokeFunc` it doesn't itself use except for delegation — currently leaks logout's internals into the auth command's signature.\n\n**9. Function-type aliases leaking** — `auth.go:26-29`. `authTokenLister` and `authTokenRevoker` are fine, but `runAuthRevoke` re-uses `logoutTokenStore` and `logoutRevokeFunc` from logout.go (auth.go:405,407). Either rename to neutral names (`tokenStore`, `revokeCurrentFunc`) in a shared file, or define an `authRevokeStore` interface in auth.go that embeds what's needed. Currently auth.go has a soft dependency on logout.go's exported (lowercased) names.\n\n**10. `fallback(s, alt)` placement** — `auth.go:359-364`. Generic 4-line helper used only in `auth.go:209-210`. Either inline it (it's used twice and is trivially `if s == \"\" { return \"-\" }`), or move to a `cli/strings.go`-style util if it has broader use. Lives correctly in auth.go for now since it's the only consumer, but the abstraction-to-usage ratio is poor.\n\n**11. PUT/PATCH/POST duplication in client.go** — `api/client.go:66-102`. `Post`, `Put`, `Patch` are byte-identical except for HTTP verb. Extract a private helper `bodyRequest(ctx, method, path, body)`. Not new in this PR but the diff touches this file so worth mentioning.\n\n**12. Double-wrapped error messages** — `api/auth_tokens.go:31,36,41`. `ListTokens` wraps every error with `\"list tokens: %w\"` even for a `c.Get()` failure that already says `\"GET /api/v1/auth/tokens: ...\"` (client.go:126). User sees `list tokens: GET /api/v1/auth/tokens: ...`. Pick one wrapping layer.\n\n**13. Test `gotAuth != testBearerHeader` constant** — `api/auth_tokens_test.go:39,104`. Good use of shared constant. No issue, just noting.\n\n**14. `_ = w.Write(...)` via nolint** — `api/auth_tokens_test.go:22,50,etc.` Spread across many lines. Consider `testutil.WriteJSON(w, body)` or fixture helper to avoid `//nolint:errcheck` salting.\n\nFiles referenced:\n- `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/auth.go`\n- `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/logout.go`\n- `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/api/auth_tokens.go`\n- `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/api/client.go`\n- `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/auth_test.go`\n- `/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/api/auth_tokens_test.go`"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a765316aaec9964c6 (use SendMessage with to: 'a765316aae