{"parentUuid":"27c86163-11a9-4edc-96d3-c0178f80228d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b2d84caf-e4de-40b4-84ec-c8e45890e57e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"**Findings**\n\n1. High: the new authenticated commands bypass the repo’s insecure-HTTP guard and will send bearer tokens over plain `http://` without any opt-in. `login` explicitly blocks this unless `--insecure-http-auth` is set ([login.go](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/login.go:46), [base_url.go](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/api/base_url.go:57)), but `auth status`, `auth list`, `auth revoke`, and the updated `logout` all call the API directly with `api.BaseURL()` and no `RequireSecureURL` check ([auth.go](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/auth.go:58), [auth.go](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/auth.go:103), [auth.go](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/auth.go:367), [logout.go](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/logout.go:29)). Anyone using `ENTIRE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:...` now transmits their stored token in cleartext.\n\n2. Medium: `entire auth revoke <id>` leaves a stale local credential behind if `<id>` is the token currently used by this CLI session. The `--current` path correctly delegates to `runLogout()` and deletes the keychain entry, but the by-ID path only calls `revokeByID()` and prints success ([auth.go](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/auth.go:397), [auth.go](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/auth.go:403)). After that, the server-side token is gone but the local keychain still contains it, so the CLI appears logged in until future commands start failing with 401s.\n\nI did not find other clear correctness issues in the diff. I also attempted a focused `go test` run, but it failed in this environment because dependency/module-cache setup is incomplete, so I couldn’t use test execution as additional validation."},"uuid":"aa35a400-5578-43a9